# Shell scripts must stay LF even on Windows checkouts (CRLF breaks the shebang).
*.sh text eol=lf
# Force LF for PowerShell too (pwsh 6+ handles LF fine on Windows).
*.ps1 text eol=lf
# Pin LF for Markdown too: the installer hashes agent .md files, and a manifest
# produced on one checkout must match re-hashing on any other (e.g. shared
# ~/.claude across WSL + Windows). CRLF normalization would diverge the hashes.
*.md   text eol=lf
# CI configs and PowerShell data files: LF for consistency.
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.psd1 text eol=lf
# Linter fixtures, expect files and eval prompts: the lint-ru awk pass matches
# line-anchored patterns (e.g. ^---$) that a trailing \r silently breaks, so a
# CRLF checkout would flip fixture results on Windows.
*.expect text eol=lf
*.txt    text eol=lf
*.html   text eol=lf
